<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Great Sword</h1>
<p>Also called: Zweihander
Two-Handed
Average Length: Approx. 4 feet
Type of Weapon: Distanced Hand-to-hand.
</p><p>The two-handed sword of medieval Europe had a number of names, most fairly self-explanatory. Great in size and weight (some weighed as much as 15-20 pounds), they required two hands to use (zweihander is German for two handed). Most simple two-handed swords were characterized by long straight blades, straight quillons, and a long hilt sufficient for grasping with two hands. Some two-handed swords such as the claymore and flamberge were unique enough to have their own names. Despite their straight blades, two-handed swords were designed for swinging, rather than just thrusting. It was one of the few swords designed to and capable of crushing through heavy armor. A great deal of strength and space were needed to use a two-handed sword well. Two-handed weapons were most popular in Germany and England (the Highlanders preferred their claymore).
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla the great sword is a weapon skill of its own, one of the swords (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): two-handed, it slashes, it leans on strength, with some dexterity, and it is slow, as two-handed weapons are. It is taught by the barbarians from guild level 25, the knights from guild level 25 and the paladins from guild level 25.
</p><p><br />
